1509	2UlZkGDvuE8	Making Isn't Manufacturing - Brady Forrest - FOSSASIA Summit 2017	2017-03-18 15:06:41	Speaker(s): Brady Forrest (San Francisco, California)\r\n\r\nAbstract:\r\nMaking something is easy; making something that can be made is hard – very hard. As the cofounder of Highway1, a hardware accelerator, I've seen many dead bodies in the early stage hardware space. Hardware takes longer, costs a lot and requires more people. It can be perilous for a company, but the rewards can be great. This talk outlines some of the funding and product development lessons that I've learned with my startups.\r\n\r\n(Type: Talk | Track: Hardware & Making | Room: Fermi (Floor 3))\r\n\r\nEvent Page: http://2017.fossasia.org\r\n\r\nProduced by Engineers.SG	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2UlZkGDvuE8/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2UlZkGDvuE8/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2UlZkGDvuE8/hqdefault.jpg	2017-03-18 15:30:59.49838	2025-02-09 14:01:05.444139	\N	t	1	87
