1449	GCKX9X1x9Uc	Bite 1 - Learn to write your first playbook with Ansible - DevOps Workshops - Bite-Sized Learning	2017-03-08 15:22:42	Speaker: Gourav Shah, Initcron Systems (@initcron)\r\n\r\nAnsible  :  Ansible is an open source configuration management, provisioning automation, application deployment and orchestration and ad hoc server management tool in one. Originally written by Michael De Hann, it's now acquired and promoted by Redhat and has an active community around it.  \r\n\r\nWhat can I do with Ansible?  •  Provision infrastructure components on cloud e.g. compute, network, storage and other managed resources such as databases, caches etc.  • Install and configure system and application configurations  •  Software  Change management •  Deploy an application, do rolling updates etc.  •  Run ad-hoc commands on a group of servers in parallel \r\n\r\nIs this for me?  This workshop is for you if,  •  You are part of the ops team (systems/operations/network/infra engineers) and would like to learn how to manage systems at scale and automate common infrastructure tasks.  • If you are a part of development organization/ DevOps team and are involved in automating application deployments and orchestration.  • If you are a QA/Test engineer and are involved in building test infrastructure/setups frequently and use scripts or manual approach to doing that.   What topic will I  learn? •  Ansible quick overview  •  The language - YAML basics •  Playbooks - writing infrastructure as a code with Ansible •  Modules  -  The playbook plugins \r\n\r\nWhat will I  do during the workshop? •  Setup a cluster of Ansible nodes with a controller and 5 managed nodes •  Write a simple playbook to install an application and start service using core modules • Deploy application to the managed nodes \r\n\r\nSlides: http://schoolofdevops.slides.com/schoolofdevops/ansible#/\r\n\r\nSource Code: https://github.com/schoolofdevops/ansible-tutorial\r\n\r\nEvent Page: https://www.meetup.com/Singapore-Devops-Workshops/events/237896364/\r\n\r\nProduced by Engineers.SG\n\nHelp us caption & translate this video!\n\nhttp://amara.org/v/4pv1/	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/GCKX9X1x9Uc/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/GCKX9X1x9Uc/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/GCKX9X1x9Uc/hqdefault.jpg	2017-03-08 15:30:57.373119	2024-09-18 16:01:11.149132	\N	t	1	2327
1599	8y0KC5mBrz8	MySQL operations in Docker - Giuseppe Maxia - FOSSASIA Summit 2017	2017-03-19 16:12:01	Speaker(s): Giuseppe Maxia (Valencia)\r\n\r\nAbstract:\r\nRunning database operations in containers is a slightly different proposition than running other services. MySQL, being designed - as the majority of services - for running in a dedicated host, needs some adjusting to fit in a container. Thanks to its configurability, we can deploy MySQL containers to fit our purposes, with just the right amount of customization. However, customizing in Docker is done differently, and we will see it in detail. This tutorial will cover :* Operations from scratch, starting with running a single container;* Steps and pitfalls of customising containers;* Data management for safety and performance;* Making several containers work together in replication;* Using containers as software transporters: mixing MySQL versions and operating systems.Attendees to this tutorial will learn the basics of using MySQL containers stand-alone and in replication.\r\n\r\n(Type: Workshop | Track: Database - MySQL Day | Room: Curie & Hershel (Floor 2))\r\n\r\nEvent Page: http://2017.fossasia.org\r\n\r\nProduced by Engineers.SG	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/8y0KC5mBrz8/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/8y0KC5mBrz8/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/8y0KC5mBrz8/hqdefault.jpg	2017-03-19 16:31:11.937737	2024-05-23 15:00:44.825712	\N	t	1	178
3874	pexJHPfOw5w	Identifying Product Opportunities with Jobs to be Done - UXSEA Summit 2019	2020-01-01 14:18:37	Speakers:\n\nNicole Bacchus\nResearch Lead Product Creation @ Instagram\n\nNicole leads the Creation Research team at Instagram, focused on sharing products including Stories, Feed, and Instagram’s camera, formats, and effects. Since completing her MBA at the Kellogg School of Management, Nicole has worn many hats in a variety of industries over the last 12 years, marrying her strong business and strategy background with her passion for rich consumer insights.\n\nFrom Brand Management at Mars Chocolate, to Innovation at American Express, and Innovation Strategy and Research at leadings strategic design consultancies, Nicole delights in driving consumer insight-led product innovation and galvanizing teams in the creation of superior customer experiences. At Instagram, Nicole leverages her strong strategic prowess to help teams translate consumer insights into actionable product strategies.\n\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/nibacchus/\n\nAlyssa Ayunan\nUser Experience Researcher @ Instagram\n\nAlyssa is a User Experience Researcher at Instagram and leads research on products like Feed and Stories. Her work focuses on guiding product strategy to ensure that people are able to connect with each other and share what matters most to them. She loves helping design and engineering teams make empathy-based decisions — from understanding users’ contexts and problem framing, all the way to testing and validating final prototypes.\n\nPrior to Instagram, Alyssa worked as a B2B user researcher, where she focused on improving enterprise workflows in ad tech and corporate banking. When she’s not in the lab, you can find Alyssa exploring Bay Area hiking trails or experimenting with new dessert recipes.\n\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/alyssaayunan\n\nEvent Page: https://uxsea.org/summit-2019\n\nProduced by Engineers.SG\n\nHelp us caption & translate this video!\n\nhttps://amara.org/v/CZaaQ/	https://i9.ytimg.com/vi/pexJHPfOw5w/default.jpg?sqp=CMjYvKwG&rs=AOn4CLCWXvAJ4w6GJn_5Msgp-t7OXhrI-w	https://i9.ytimg.com/vi/pexJHPfOw5w/mqdefault.jpg?sqp=CMjYvKwG&rs=AOn4CLCX6Sl_l5uS1pppCn4PbIwo17crFg	https://i9.ytimg.com/vi/pexJHPfOw5w/hqdefault.jpg?sqp=CMjYvKwG&rs=AOn4CLAdV8Vtv1ImgYbZv-t8OX4v8fKBcA	2020-01-01 14:32:29.17891	2023-12-29 20:31:13.055629	\N	f	1	53
