1217	lJlyR8chDwo	Build Features, Not Apps - iOS Conf SG 2016	2016-10-23 03:32:56	Speaker: Natasha Murashev - @NatashaTheRobot\n\nMost iPhone users don’t bother installing any apps per months. And worse, ~80% never use an app they’ve installed again. The future of mobile is clearly not app, but features. Features that make the iPhone ecosystem still a native experience, but as open and flexible as the web. Learn how you could prepare for that future.\n\nAbout the speaker\n\nNatasha is an iOS developer by day and a robot by night. She blogs about Swift, watchOS, and iOS development on her blog, natashatherobot.com, curates a fast-growing weekly Swift newsletter, This Week in Swift, and organizes the try! Swift Conference around the world. She's currently living the digital nomad life as her alter identity: @NatashaTheNomad\n\nEvent URL: http://iosconf.sg/\n\nProduced by Engineers.SG	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lJlyR8chDwo/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lJlyR8chDwo/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lJlyR8chDwo/hqdefault.jpg	2016-10-23 03:35:32.062045	2025-01-08 18:01:11.30625	\N	t	1	2397
2564	xboIoFDuB5U	Insta-QRP Open Hardware Transceiver Kit for the Amateur Band - Joyce Ng - FOSSASIA 2018	2018-04-13 15:02:42	Speaker: Joyce Ng\nInfo: https://2018.fossasia.org/event/speakers.html#joyce-ng3335\n\n"We use radio communications systems everyday technologies such as Wi-Fi Bluetooth 3G 4G and many more are an integral part of our society today. However do we understand how they work? The Insta-QRP Radio Transceiver is a open-hardware radio transceiver kit that aims to demonstrate the concepts of radio transmission and reception."\n\n(Type: Talk | Track: Science Tech | Room: Event Hall 2-2)\n\nEvent Page: http://2018.fossasia.org\nFollow FOSSASIA on Twitter: https://twitter.com/fossasia/\nLike FOSSASIA on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/fossasia/ \n\nProduced by Engineers.SG	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/xboIoFDuB5U/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/xboIoFDuB5U/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/xboIoFDuB5U/hqdefault.jpg	2018-04-13 15:30:50.503927	2025-01-19 14:01:35.162532	\N	t	1	120
