1797	4MDTBBEEyho	IT Holy Wars by Guillaume Laforge	2017-06-15 18:01:47	The biggest challenge of Deep Learning technology is the scalability. As long as using single GPU server, you have to wait for hours or days to get the result of your work. This doesn’t scale for production service, so you need a Distributed Training on the cloud eventually. Google has been building infrastructure for training the large scale neural network on the cloud for years, and now started to share the technology with external developers. In this session, we will introduce new pre-trained ML services such as Cloud Vision API and Speech API that works without any training. Also, we will look how TensorFlow and Cloud Machine Learning will accelerate custom model training for 10x – 40x with Google’s distributed training infrastructure.\n\nGuillaume Laforge is a Developer Advocate at @Google for @GoogleCloud during the day, and @ApacheGroovy programming language project PMC Chair at night.	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/4MDTBBEEyho/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/4MDTBBEEyho/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/4MDTBBEEyho/hqdefault.jpg	2017-06-19 14:25:20.389302	2025-02-06 16:01:05.228649	\N	t	1	763
2566	vCcmbkVfcSA	Building a Sustainable Open Tech Community: Coding Programs, Contests and Hackathons - FOSSASIA 2018	2018-04-13 15:46:07	Panelists: \n- Hong Phuc Dang: https://2018.fossasia.org/event/speakers.html#hong-phuc-dang3041\n- Stephanie Taylor: https://2018.fossasia.org/event/speakers.html#stephanie-taylor3288\n- Victoria Bondarchuk: https://2018.fossasia.org/event/speakers.html#victoria-bondarchuk3363\n- Damini Satya: https://2018.fossasia.org/event/speakers.html#damini-satya3344\n- Yue Lin Choong: https://2018.fossasia.org/event/speakers.html#yue-lin-choong3072\n\nHow sustainable is it do build open tech communities through coding programs, contests and hackathons? What is the experience of Google Summer of Code, Codeheat, Google Code-in, UN Volunteers, Hacktoberfest, 24PRs? What goals do programs have? Are they achieving the goal of advancing Open Tech projects? Panel with Hong Phuc Dang, Misako, Stephanie Taylor, Gi Soong Chee.\n\n(Type: Panel | Track: Science Tech | Room: Event Hall 2-2)\n\nEvent Page: http://2018.fossasia.org\nFollow FOSSASIA on Twitter: https://twitter.com/fossasia/\nLike FOSSASIA on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/fossasia/ \n\nProduced by Engineers.SG	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/vCcmbkVfcSA/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/vCcmbkVfcSA/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/vCcmbkVfcSA/hqdefault.jpg	2018-04-13 16:32:04.09427	2025-01-20 21:01:30.913528	\N	t	1	228
