2430	HPzkf_qHuSo	Delivering a bleeding edge community-led openstack distribution: RDO - Chandan Kumar - FOSSASIA 2018	2018-03-25 04:16:13	Speaker: Chandan Kumar\nInfo: https://2018.fossasia.org/event/speakers.html#chandan-kumar3305\n\nOpenStack is complex with lots of services and choices to deploy your own cloud in any fashion.\n\nDeploying OpenStack from sources is hard. RDO is an OpenStack community distribution for RHEL/CentOS and friends.\n\nRDO make it possible by delivering latest RPM packages with the help of different deployment tools by chasing trunk through different CI/CD with in days from upstream release.\n\nThis talk is about:\n\n* A little history about RDO\n\n* How they used to release vanilla OpenStack 2 years back.\n\n* How they reached two days time frame on releasing RDO after upstream openstack releases through different CI/CD and proper testing.\n\n* How Ansible and Upstream OpenStack tools (zuul gerrit nodepool ARA CentOS Infra software factory) made it possible?\n\n* Making OpenStack usable to work out of the box through Tripleo Puppet Kolla CI\n\n* Making it easy for installers to test against latest upstream code so that they can\n\n  Get released shortly after the services.\n\n* How we are making OpenStack better through RDO?\n\n* How you can also contribute in making it better?\n\nTrack: Cloud, Container, DevOps\nRoom: Event Hall 1-1\nDate: Sunday, 25th March, 2018\n\nEvent Page: http://2018.fossasia.org\nFollow FOSSASIA on Twitter: https://twitter.com/fossasia/\nLike FOSSASIA on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/fossasia/\n\nProduced by Engineers.SG	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/HPzkf_qHuSo/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/HPzkf_qHuSo/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/HPzkf_qHuSo/hqdefault.jpg	2018-03-25 04:30:48.274312	2024-04-10 11:00:46.041259	\N	t	1	78
