58	Y1WtulpJEuI	Collaborate with ease and Confidence - Georg Greve - FOSSASIA Summit 2015	2015-03-17 06:10:06	Speaker: Georg Greve, Kolab Systems AG\n\nDescription:\nCommunication and collaboration are the life blood of our professional world. Kolab is the comprehensive solution that enables collaboration across all platforms and with great ease. Based on a micro service architecture, it can integrate into environment or cloud strategy, and is the only solution of its kind that was built for highest levels of security from the ground up thanks to its origins with the German Federal Office for IT Security. It's use cases range from self-hosting on a Raspberry Pi to multiple data centres serving millions of users with advanced Audit, eDiscovery and Data Loss Prevention (DLP) scenarios. Kolab is also available as Kolab Now, a public service similar to Google Apps or Hotmail.com, but hosted in Switzerland under enhanced privacy provisions for professionals who cannot afford to compromise the data and communication of their customers and partners.\n\nProduced by Engineers.SG	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Y1WtulpJEuI/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Y1WtulpJEuI/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Y1WtulpJEuI/hqdefault.jpg	2015-05-07 15:32:30.847782	2023-05-29 04:00:50.078785	214	t	1	65
3365	cYNblil509o	Traveloka x DSSG: NLP & Personalised Recommendations (Part 2)	2019-05-18 05:11:34	Links to slides:\r\nhttps://www.facebook.com/download/2681636338530622/2019-05-16-DSSG_dynamic-personalised-recommendations-yuxuan.pdf\r\n\r\nhttps://www.facebook.com/download/690594354728951/2019-05-16-DSSG_BahasaNLP_Presentation_Deb.pdf\r\n\r\nAbstract 1:\r\nIn this talk, Deb Goswami (Data Science Lead at Traveloka) will walk through challenges in enabling high quality NLP for low resource languages such as Bahasa. These challenges include using word2vec (Transfer learning + Vanilla), Data Quality, Issues, Various types of LSTM results, Transition into Char-level embeddings, or types of ML metrics to use, as well as challenges in production.\r\n\r\nSpeaker 1 Bio:\r\n\r\nDr. Deb Goswami is a seasoned Machine Learning practitioner, with over 10 years of research and production experience into enabling large-scale AI systems.\r\nHe is currently building out data science at Traveloka, Indonesia's leading multi-billion dollar travel unicorn, where his teams are responsible for delivering advanced machine learning capabilities in Natural Language Processing, Computer Vision, Speech and Personalisation.\r\n\r\nPrior to this, he has worked on production AI solutions across a variety of industries ranging from Oil and Gas, Telecoms, E-commerce and Advertising.\r\n\r\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/debgoswami/\r\n\r\nAbstract 2:\r\n*Dynamic Personalised Recommendations: Data and Algorithms*\r\nIn this talk, Yu Xuan will be sharing the Smart Adaptive Recommendations algorithm. It can be used to serve both item similarity recommendations and dynamic personalised recommendations. Despite this, it is very straightforward conceptually and is a useful baseline for personalised recommendations. He will cover the data required, the models used and some implementation details.\r\n\r\nSpeaker 2 Bio:\r\n\r\nYu Xuan has more than 5 years experience working in Data Science and Machine Learning Engineering. He is currently a Data Scientist in Traveloka where he builds ranking and recommendation systems for products across Traveloka businesses. Previously, he has worked in Lazada and GovTech, handling data science problems in various domain such as language, images and fraud.\r\n\r\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/yxtay/\r\nEvent Page: \r\n\r\nProduced by Engineers.SG\n\nHelp us caption & translate this video!\n\nhttps://amara.org/v/ov2J/	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/cYNblil509o/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/cYNblil509o/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/cYNblil509o/hqdefault.jpg	2019-05-18 05:31:29.119405	2024-11-23 22:01:48.862347	\N	t	1	104
1224	YuPM_I9bQMI	Swift for IoT - iOS Conf SG 2016	2016-10-23 03:33:36	Speaker:  Subhransu Behera (@subhransu) & Kheng Meng Yeo (@yeokm1) - Singapore Power\n\nEver since Swift became open source, developers worldwide are thinking of new ways to use the language. It's being used currently in backend, some developers are thinking about building native Android apps in Swift. But the thing that got us thinking is, "Can we use Swift for IoT projects". More specifically how much can we leverage on the language features to build a Swift-only home automation system. \n\nApparently we are not alone, there are other people working already in this field and have built cool stuff on Raspberry Pi and BeagleBone using Swift. This talk will focus the essntials on running Swift on BeagleBone and how to work with peripheral devices and sensors. We will discuss about the Swift features that worked really well while working on this project and share what are the opportunities for future.\n\nAbout the speakers\n\nSubh is a lead mobile developer at Singapore Power. Prior to Singapore Power, he worked at PayPal where he was leading an iOS team and was instrumental in developing the revamped iOS app of PayPal. \n\nHe is the organizer of iOS Conf SG and runs iOS Dev Scout, the iOS developer and meetup group in Singapore. He contributed to the popular iOS tutorial site, RayWenderlich.com.\n\nKheng Meng is a maker in the areas of electronics, embedded programming and hardware. He is working as an IoT engineer at Singapore Power. At his previous job at Algo Access he built a hardware providing solutions to eye-care professionals.\n\nOutside work, he loves to share his knowledge and learning experiences of his projects by participating in talks and meetups.\n\nEvent URL: http://iosconf.sg/\n\nProduced by Engineers.SG	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/YuPM_I9bQMI/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/YuPM_I9bQMI/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/YuPM_I9bQMI/hqdefault.jpg	2016-10-23 03:35:32.190046	2025-02-06 07:01:04.498693	\N	t	1	2005
2463	btoCB6smoMs	Enhanced XA Support for Replication in MySQL-5.7 - Nisha Gopalakrishnan - FOSSASIA 2018	2018-03-25 07:54:44	Speaker: Nisha Gopalakrishnan\nInfo: https://2018.fossasia.org/event/speakers.html#nisha-gopalakrishnan3141\n\nXA stands for “eXtended Architecture”, and is a standard   created by The Open Group for distributed    transaction processing. XA addresses the problem of preserving ACID   properties within a single transaction across a distributed set of resources. The resources   themselves could be other MySQL servers, or even different database technologies. MySQL 5.0   introduced XA support, thus adding the ability to participate in global transactions. MySQL 5.7 has removed   major limitations in the XA transaction recovery mechanism and binary logging mechanism.      This talk would cover the following points:   * What is XA?   * How does MySQL support the XA standard?   * How to perform XA transactions in MySQL.   * Improvement made in 5.7 for XA transaction recovery.   * Improvement made to use XA transaction safely with replication.\n\nTrack: Database\nRoom: Training room 2-1\nDate: Sunday, 25th March, 2018\n\nEvent Page: http://2018.fossasia.org\nFollow FOSSASIA on Twitter: https://twitter.com/fossasia/\nLike FOSSASIA on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/fossasia/\n\nProduced by Engineers.SG	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/btoCB6smoMs/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/btoCB6smoMs/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/btoCB6smoMs/hqdefault.jpg	2018-03-25 08:31:02.315404	2025-02-17 16:01:18.844819	\N	t	1	570
1403	yBejNknFHRo	Getting started with editing a VR 360 video - Creative Crew	2017-02-14 14:59:28	Speaker: Lynus Hee\n\nWith the increasing popularity and different application of 360 VR, it is important to discuss an import issue that comes naturally with video: Editing. Ever since the first continuity cut was used in 1898 by Rober W. Paul, there has been a development of rules in film montage in which film makers “abide by” such as the 180 degree rule and match action cuts. \n\nSpeaker Lynus Hee has recently been concluded a year-long research into this area of 360 VR video editing and will share his findings. So if you don’t have anyone to celebrate Valentine’s day with, head on down to Toa Payoh Library at 7p.m.\n\nEvent Page: https://www.facebook.com/events/1797368173846126\n\nProduced by Engineers.SG\n\nHelp us caption & translate this video!\n\nhttp://amara.org/v/4HYe/	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/yBejNknFHRo/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/yBejNknFHRo/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/yBejNknFHRo/hqdefault.jpg	2017-02-14 15:31:08.754282	2024-11-08 02:01:21.035371	\N	t	1	112
4160	q3Z0iFRZrdE	Improve developer experience with Github Actions - SingaporeJS	2020-10-21 13:43:50	Speaker: Sergey Golovin\ngithub: @daynin\ntwitter: https://twitter.com/_sgolovin\n\nThis talk about how we improved our developer experience in CSSSR (https://csssr.com/en) with Github Actions. What we used before to automate linting, testing, building, and deploying all our projects. How GH Actions make it easier to build development workflows and what you can automate with them (almost everything).\n\nPresenter's bio\nHi, I'm Sergey Golovin. Software Engineer at CSSSR. I'm a big fan of open source, contributor in some projects, podcaster and co-organizer of a developers community\n\r\nEvent Page: https://github.com/SingaporeJS/talk.js/issues/42\r\n\r\nProduced by Engineers.SG\r\nRecorded by: Michael Cheng	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/q3Z0iFRZrdE/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/q3Z0iFRZrdE/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/q3Z0iFRZrdE/hqdefault.jpg	2020-10-21 14:32:35.26763	2025-02-13 12:01:42.325407	\N	t	1	219
