2662	awEqPxDW9og	Get better at Refactoring - Voxxed Days Singapore 2018	2018-06-11 09:46:11	Speaker: Stanly Lau (ODD-E)\n\nYou have found the more you change the code, the more difficult it becomes. Refactoring is a developer practice of improving the internal structure of existing code without changing the external behaviour. It makes code changes for present or future easier. You may have heard about Refactoring from colleagues, books, articles and have probably tried or hear it the first time. This talk presents what it is, why it is important and what you can do to get better at it based on the experience of mentoring on technical practices to others. This talk is suitable for people who are experienced in programming, have met the challenges of making changes and want to deepen their skill. Demo included!\n\nStanly is a software development coach in Odd-e, helping companies to grow self-managing teams and technical practices. He grew up in Singapore and started programming professionally since ten years ago. He has a deep interest in helping developers to increase their competence in technical skills and has spent many years mentoring teams. He is also the early founders of Agile community in Singapore and organiser of the Agile Singapore conferences.	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/awEqPxDW9og/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/awEqPxDW9og/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/awEqPxDW9og/hqdefault.jpg	2018-06-11 14:59:03.36301	2025-02-05 20:01:37.239614	\N	t	1	676
787	f19cKxYr5yQ	Panel: Digital Health in Singapore - Digital Health Singapore Meetup	2016-06-17 05:57:36	Digital Health in Singapore: Present and Future\r\n\r\nPanelists:\r\n\r\nMerck - Michelle Mosolgo, CTO at HSS\r\nCXA Group - Rosaline Koo, CEO\r\nMyDoc - Snehal Patel, CEO\r\nFormer Health Sciences Authority consultant - Leng Teng\r\n\r\nWhile the need for quality healthcare is undeniable, are consumers substituting Dr Google for their doctors, or are they measuring their blood pressure and ECG at home? And how do doctors and hospitals view the 'consumerization' of healthcare as wellness product are increasingly sold over-the-counter?\r\nThe Digital Health Meetup is series of gatherings held at various Asian cities. It aims to bring together healthcare professionals, engineers, startups, investors, regulatory bodies and corporate executives, so as to facilitate dialogue on overcoming challenges at health systems with technology. \r\n\r\nEvent Page: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/digital-health-singapore-meetup-tickets-25772384897\r\n\r\nProduced by Engineers.SG\r\n\r\nHelp us caption & translate this video!\r\n\r\nhttp://amara.org/v/Mr89/	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/f19cKxYr5yQ/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/f19cKxYr5yQ/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/f19cKxYr5yQ/hqdefault.jpg	2016-06-17 05:59:28.492616	2024-03-27 23:00:21.097856	\N	f	1	478
