4296	9dsLFse9IyA	The Internet of Value: Digital Assets with Java - Singapore Java User Group	2021-05-08 01:14:24	Speaker: Mike Anderson\n\n== Talk\nDigital assets are poised to change the world, with decentralised cryptocurrencies, non-fungible tokens (NFTs) and smart contracts creating new opportunities for economic value exchange and product innovation: a space which might be called "The Internet of Value".\n\nConvex (https://convex.world/) is a full-stack solution for the Internet of Value, built using Java technology and offering radically better performance than traditional blockchain approaches.\n\nIn this talk we will look at the principles of creating digital assets for the Internet of Value, explain the inner workings of Convex and demonstrate how to build your own digital assets using a simple Java API for the Convex network.\n\n== Speaker\nMike is the Managing Director of The Convex Foundation, a non-profit organisation dedicated to helping organisations realize the potential of decentralised ledger technology for the Internet of Value. He is the inventor of the Convergent Proof of Stake consensus algorithm, which forms the basis for the Convex network.\n\nPreviously, Mike has held CTO roles at multiple companies, with a focus on blockchain, data science and AI. He also worked as a strategy consultant at McKinsey and company, specialising in software architecture, technology strategy and healthcare IT.\n\nMike is a keen open source software developer, and contributes his time to leading multiple open source projects, especially in the Clojure and Java ecosystems. He is the creator of core.matrix, a library for advanced numerical algorithms.\n\nMike holds double first in Mathematics and Economics from Cambridge University, and a Master of Business Administration (with Distinction) from INSEAD. He formerly represented the UK in the International Olympiad in Informatics.\r\n\nEvent Page: https://www.meetup.com/singajug/events/277316614/\r\n\r\nProduced by Engineers.SG\r\nRecorded by: Michael	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/9dsLFse9IyA/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/9dsLFse9IyA/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/9dsLFse9IyA/hqdefault.jpg	2021-05-08 01:31:22.815904	2025-02-16 10:01:43.273079	\N	t	1	232
1142	cT0mP0DtKzM	Gary Guwe  - Fuckup Nights Singapore	2016-10-05 22:35:00	Speaker: Gary Guwe, Co-founder of Catalyst Empowerment, Author of The Shy Speakers Guide blog\n\nGary is a serial-entrepreneur and Co-founder of Speak! Ventures and Catalyst Empowerment Pte Ltd. He is also a published author & coach specialising in the Authoritative Art of Influence.\nGary first began his training career at the age of 21 and a career spanning over 10 years has seen him speak to over 20,000 individuals in different parts of the world. At the age of 27, he was headhunted to work with business leaders representing billion-dollar brands like Google, HP, Siemens & Microsoft, and has since gone on to lecture at two of the world's top universities. His blog The Shy Speakers Guide is ranked amongst the top #26 in the entire world. Gary has appeared on various media, such as The Straits Times, The New Paper, 938Live and even Lifehack.org.\nIn spite of these, the journey hasn't always been a smooth and storm-free one. Find out more about his tale of chasing his dreams in business, losing way, and finally founding himself... and his insights on what matters most as we pursue our dreams and build a business.\n\nEvent Page: http://www.eventbrite.com/e/fuckup-nights-singapore-vol-xii-tickets-27223871332\n\nProduced by Engineers.SG\n\nHelp us caption & translate this video!\n\nhttp://amara.org/v/WkSs/	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/cT0mP0DtKzM/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/cT0mP0DtKzM/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/cT0mP0DtKzM/hqdefault.jpg	2016-10-05 22:35:40.496484	2024-12-25 15:01:24.460427	\N	t	1	202
3400	WtUtVaCnnZc	Google Cloud Next Singapore 2019: Moving people and products with Machine Learning on Kubeflow	2019-06-01 07:40:01	Synopsis: GOJEK, the Southeast Asian super app, has experienced a massive increase in customer growth by leveraging machine learning throughout its products. However, building production grade machine learning systems is still fraught with challenges and delays. In order to address these challenges GOJEK has adopted Kubeflow, a fully open source cloud native platform for machine learning.\r\nIn this talk you will learn how Kubernetes and Kubeflow empowers teams at GOJEK by increasing the speed at which they turn ideas into products. We will show how Kubeflow, which leverages Kubernetes and Istio, simplifies the process of rapidly training, deploying, and evaluating models.\r\n\r\nSpeaker: Willem Pienaar leads the data science platform team at GOJEK, working on the GOJEK ML platform, which supports a wide variety of models and handles hundreds of million of orders every month. His main focus areas are building data and ML platforms, allowing organizations to scale machine learning and drive decision making.\r\n\r\nEvent Page: https://www.meetup.com/GCPUGSG/events/258359490/\r\n\r\nRecorded By: Allan A. Chua (http://www.pogsdotnet.com/)\r\nProduced by Engineers.SG\n\nHelp us caption & translate this video!\n\nhttps://amara.org/v/pJ7m/	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/WtUtVaCnnZc/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/WtUtVaCnnZc/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/WtUtVaCnnZc/hqdefault.jpg	2019-06-01 08:31:42.456331	2024-10-22 18:01:35.77564	\N	t	1	152
3012	u5K9sJhuq6I	YOW! Singapore 2018 - Jeff Patton - MVP: and Why We Confuse Building to Learn with Building to Earn	2018-10-24 05:56:13	The minimum viable product is one of the most misunderstood, misused, and abused terms in contemporary software development. In this talk, Jeff will explain the misunderstandings made by thought leaders that lead to the confusion we all deal with today. You’ll learn the counter-intuitive concepts hidden in the term and why really using them is so hard. You’ll learn about techniques that will ultimately help you find smaller successful releases, test your ideas faster, develop higher quality software more predictably, and release more confidently than ever before. Because hidden in this nasty little term are clues that can help you do all that.\n\nFor more on YOW! Conference visit: https://www.yowconference.com.au and for details: https://www.yowconference.sg/profile/?id=jeff-patton	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/u5K9sJhuq6I/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/u5K9sJhuq6I/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/u5K9sJhuq6I/hqdefault.jpg	2018-11-26 13:16:12.764396	2023-10-18 08:02:00.077132	\N	t	1	482
