783	bcmv_k1_cmI	Getting Started with 360 Video and Virtual Reality - Creative Crew Singapore	2016-06-16 15:43:28	Speaker:  Lionel Chok\n\nNo one could have guessed what was on Mark Zuckerberg's mind when Facebook acquired Oculus for $2 billion back in 2014. Not until a year later, when 360 videos became a news feed feature on Facebook's wall, Google Cardboards shipped over 5 million; and Virtual Reality became a buzz word across industries and investors.\n\nJust what is the hype behind 360 and Virtual Reality? More importantly - can you be part of it? How technical is the progress and what does it entail?\n\nIn this hour-long session, VR Technologist Lionel Chok will attempt to answer some of the above, demo some of his works, as well as how to get you started in the live action 360 and VR space, plus also differentiate those in CG, Animation and Gaming.\n\nEvent Page: https://www.facebook.com/events/1547724118867473\n\nProduced by Engineers.SG\n\nHelp us caption & translate this video!\n\nhttp://amara.org/v/MlfO/	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/bcmv_k1_cmI/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/bcmv_k1_cmI/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/bcmv_k1_cmI/hqdefault.jpg	2016-06-16 16:03:42.831938	2025-01-03 13:01:04.841565	\N	t	1	96
3835	Ff9--bQiv3c	Developer's Gym - Zero to Kubernetes - JuniorDevSG - Bad edit	2019-12-07 16:05:52	Speaker: Daniele Polencic\n\nYou've heard of Docker and Kubernetes, and you can tell that they are the next big thing to learn.\n\nYou want to master Kubernetes, but where should you start?\n\nEnter Zero to Kubernetes: a step-by-step course on how to architect, develop and deploy applications in Kubernetes.\n\nThis course walks you through the full path from coding an application to deploying it to a production-grade Kubernetes cluster.\n\n## You will learn how to\n\n- Write a note-taking application in Node.js or Java\n- Package the app as a Docker image\n- Deploy the containerised application to a local Minikube cluster\n- Refactor your application to make it stateless and scalable\n- Deploy the improved application to a production-grade Kubernetes cluster on AWS\n\n## This workshop is for\n\n- Docker and Kubernetes beginners\n- Developers who build and architect cloud-native applications\n- DevOps and system administrators\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Java or Node.js installed\n- Minikube and kubectl\n- Docker\n- Git, curl\n\nThis workshop is Windows, macOS and Ubuntu friendly.\n\nYou will be using the Learnk8s Academy for this workshop. You will need a valid email address to access the content.\n\n## About the trainer\n\nDaniele is an instructor at Learnk8s, where he teaches Kubernetes and containers to small and large enterprises.\n\nEvent Page: https://www.meetup.com/Junior-Developers-Singapore/events/266312516/\n\nProduced by Engineers.SG\nRecorded by: Michael	https://i9.ytimg.com/vi/Ff9--bQiv3c/default.jpg?sqp=CMjYvKwG&rs=AOn4CLCGocpSz592cF9IyqC0ZW1fOK3J1A	https://i9.ytimg.com/vi/Ff9--bQiv3c/mqdefault.jpg?sqp=CMjYvKwG&rs=AOn4CLDLXZAgiEYqBuQwxAh08YbmXE5Clg	https://i9.ytimg.com/vi/Ff9--bQiv3c/hqdefault.jpg?sqp=CMjYvKwG&rs=AOn4CLCNV07vpk9XeP3Vo3DV45-vf10_XQ	2019-12-08 02:32:36.700528	2023-12-29 20:30:51.921184	\N	f	1	82
