548	z5ruezrO9_o	Applications of data science in insurance industry - DataScienceSG	2016-02-28 07:55:19	Philippe Marie-Jeanne is a graduate engineer of the Polytechnique School, but also graduated from the National school of Statistic and Economic Administration (ENSAE) and member of the French Actuary Institute (IAF). He also follow an INSEAD executive program in 2006 (Programme supérieur pour Dirigeants).Before being Head of the Data Innovation Lab (Axa Group) that he created on January 2014, Philippe Marie-Jeanne was Group Head of P&C Retail since 2011. Before joining AXA Global P&C, Philippe Marie-Jeanne was since February 2007 P&C Technical Head at AXA France. \n\nEvent Page: http://www.meetup.com/DataScience-SG-Singapore/events/228743258/\n\nProduced by Engineers.SG\n\nHelp us caption & translate this video!\n\nhttp://amara.org/v/WCdj/	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/z5ruezrO9_o/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/z5ruezrO9_o/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/z5ruezrO9_o/hqdefault.jpg	2016-02-28 07:56:42.492877	2025-01-12 16:01:14.398877	\N	t	1	1646
4414	FOxoQjBA4pk	📸 📸 A picture is worth a thousand…kilobytes	2023-03-22 12:48:32	Speaker: Tamas Piros\r\n\r\nEvent Page: https://www.meetup.com/singapore-js/events/292267655/\r\n\r\n📸 📸 A picture is worth a thousand…kilobytes. - Tamas Piros\r\n\r\nAbout the talk:\r\nA picture is in fact worth a thousand words, but it should not be worth a thousand kilobytes. In this talk we will take a look at tips and tricks that will enable you to deliver image heavy websites in a performant way. We will discuss the pros and cons of “next-gen” image formats, the various available loading methods and techniques and their effects on the Largest Contentful Paint and Cumulative Layout Shift Core Web Vital metrics. By the end of the talk you will be equipped with the right knowledge to deliver production sites with images that perform well to maximise user retention.\r\n\r\nAbout the speaker:\r\nTamas is a Google Developer Expert in Web Technologies and a seasoned Developer Evangelist. He is a passionate advocate for modern web technologies, helping people understand and unlock the latest & greatest features of web development.\r\n\r\nMore details on the GitHub issue for this event.\r\n\r\nProduced by Engineers.SG	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/FOxoQjBA4pk/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/FOxoQjBA4pk/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/FOxoQjBA4pk/hqdefault.jpg	2023-03-22 13:33:02.505948	2024-11-21 00:02:26.744572	\N	t	1	103
1584	iG2KCDJv7SI	MySQL Replication: Latest Developments - FOSSASIA 2017	2017-03-19 14:06:14	Speaker(s): Sujatha Sivakumar (BANGALORE)\r\n\r\nAbstract:\r\nThe MySQL Replication Team at ORACLE has been striving to provide community with great replication features. It is time to celebrate again. This talk aims at providing a brief overview of all the awesome features that are available as part of MySQL-5.7.They cover a lot of different technical areas, with special emphasis on: Usability/Online: Online Reconfiguration of “Global Transaction Identifiers”, Online reconfiguration of “Replication Filters” and Online fail over to a new master. Improved replication monitoring which is more flexible and user friendly.Performance: Improved “User threads – Sender threads” synchronization, Locking based parallelism, new “Ack Receiver” thread which makes “Semi – sync Replication” faster and a faster “Sender Thread”.Dependability: “Loss-less Semi – Sync Replication” and “Wait for multiple acks”.Flexibility: Storing “Global Transaction Identifiers” in a Table and “Multi – source Replication”.Moreover, development continues and the team already has some very interesting feature previews on labs, such as a new and exciting replication plugin: MySQL Group Replication. Seize the opportunity to get together with some of the engineers behind the product and learn about the exciting new replication world in MySQL 5.7 and beyond.\r\n\r\n(Type: Talk | Track: Database - MySQL Day | Room: Curie & Hershel (Floor 2))\r\n\r\nEvent Page: http://2017.fossasia.org\r\n\r\nProduced by Engineers.SG\n\nHelp us caption & translate this video!\n\nhttp://amara.org/v/5L43/	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/iG2KCDJv7SI/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/iG2KCDJv7SI/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/iG2KCDJv7SI/hqdefault.jpg	2017-03-19 14:30:54.20763	2024-10-31 21:01:14.108919	\N	t	1	114
3477	fiCQM4L4etU	Resilient Microservices Architecture with Kubernetes - Voxxed Days Singapore 2019	2019-06-29 03:25:52	Speaker: Nilesh Gule (Prudential)\n\nNilesh is a Software Architect with a passion for technology.\n\nHe is a lifelong learner with a simple motto of “Code with Passion and Strive for Excellence”. He has a strong background in technology and keen interest in code quality. He is currently exploring Cloud computing, Microservices, containers and DevOps. When not thinking and talking about technology, he likes to watch the game of Cricket.\n\nNilesh was one of the most popular speakers in Voxxed Days Singapore 2018 (see his talk here).\n\nHe blogs at https://www.handsonarchitect.com/ .\n\nResilient Microservices Architecture with Kubernetes\n\nMicroservices architecture is becoming quite common nowadays.\nMicroservices have been around for some time, but container technologies are helping organisations to adopt new tools and techniques at a much faster pace. The talk will demonstrate how to build resilient Microservices using specific design patterns. Some of the patterns we will cover:\n\n1 – Timeout design patterns\n\n2 – Circuit breaker design pattern\n\n3 – Retry design pattern\n\n4 – Bulkheads design pattern\n\nEvent Website: https://voxxeddays.com/singapore/	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/fiCQM4L4etU/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/fiCQM4L4etU/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/fiCQM4L4etU/hqdefault.jpg	2019-07-01 06:32:54.218613	2025-01-26 15:01:13.570457	\N	t	1	1294
