1140	bk6HhR3F9Bg	Mrinalini Venkatachalam - Fuckup Nights Singapore	2016-10-05 22:35:09	Speaker: Mrinalini Venkatachalam, Head of Public Education and Youth Initiatives for UN Women (Singapore)\n\nMrinalini Venkatachalam aims to empower disadvantaged women through generating widespread awareness. As Head of Public Education and Youth Initiatives at the Singapore Committee for UN Women, she coordinates activities that shine a light on oft neglected women’s issues such the many roles of women in society, respect for migrant women in the house, the incidence of violence against women, trafficking of women and children and other issues that affect us all. Mrinalini also sits on the boards of One Singapore, an organization dedicated to raising public awareness and taking concrete actions to create The World We Want and Make Poverty History and Primetime, a network that empowers professional women in Singapore, by providing opportunities to build knowledge and skills, develop strong and collaborative networks and to contribute to community outreach programmes.\n\nEvent Page: http://www.eventbrite.com/e/fuckup-nights-singapore-vol-xii-tickets-27223871332\n\nProduced by Engineers.SG\n\nHelp us caption & translate this video!\n\nhttp://amara.org/v/WkSu/	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/bk6HhR3F9Bg/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/bk6HhR3F9Bg/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/bk6HhR3F9Bg/hqdefault.jpg	2016-10-05 22:35:40.461961	2024-11-23 01:01:00.621629	\N	t	1	539
3464	ayrw9VB5VxE	Learn how OpenID Connect and JWTs make your life easy again! - Singapore Identity & Security Meetup	2019-06-26 15:03:01	Speaker: Ben Dechrai\r\n\r\nThe Singapore Identity and Security Meetup is an informal evening open to all. We start with food, drink, and mingling, followed by a talk. The evening ends with an optional networking session at a local venue.\r\n\r\n## Talk Abstract\r\nAuthentication for a simple site is easy. A user table with permission flags. Add scaling, a service-oriented architecture, and new technology stacks and you quickly introduce complexity. Learn how OpenID Connect and JSON Web Tokens make your life easy again!\r\n\r\nThis talk includes a history of OAuth and OpenID Connect, describes the login flow, and finished with a quick demo of what it looks like to use an off-the-shelf identity provider.\r\n\r\n## Speaker Bio\r\nBen Dechrai is a technologist with a staunch focus on security and privacy. This started at the age of 11 when he wrote software to stop his mum from breaking the family PC, and resulted in his working as a developer evangelist for Auth0. He enjoys helping developers find the joy of experimentation, from ethical skulduggery to subversive automation, and can be found on Twitter and Instagram at @bendechrai.\r\n\r\nEvent Page: https://www.meetup.com/Singapore-Identity-and-Security-Meetup/events/261756509/\r\n\r\nProduced by Engineers.SG\n\nHelp us caption & translate this video!\n\nhttps://amara.org/v/pesW/	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/ayrw9VB5VxE/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/ayrw9VB5VxE/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/ayrw9VB5VxE/hqdefault.jpg	2019-06-26 15:33:00.80248	2024-07-23 21:01:43.03589	\N	t	1	129
