1569	X8pvEIn-I04	Deploy Open Event Organizer Server - FOSSASIA 2017	2017-03-19 14:06:04	Speaker(s): Saptak Sengupta (Allahabad)\r\n\r\nAbstract:\r\nOpen Event Organizer Server is a complete event management system which anyone can use to host their own events. In this talk, we will get to know how to setup the server over google cloud and local system for you to use it individually.\r\n\r\n(Type: Workshop | Track: Web & Mobile | Room: Fermi (Floor 3))\r\n\r\nEvent Page: http://2017.fossasia.org\r\n\r\nProduced by Engineers.SG\n\nHelp us caption & translate this video!\n\nhttp://amara.org/v/5LWd/	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/X8pvEIn-I04/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/X8pvEIn-I04/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/X8pvEIn-I04/hqdefault.jpg	2017-03-19 14:30:53.877883	2025-01-10 22:01:20.296365	\N	t	1	209
3804	wdFUqopfPEY	NUS Hackers - Friday Hacks #185: Succinct proofs for scaling computation on the blockchain	2019-11-15 11:07:01	Speaker: Ying Tong\n\nVerifying block transactions is computationally intensive and creates a throughput bottleneck for blockchain nodes. One area of active research in blockchain scalability is verifiable computation: this is where heavy computations are outsourced to a third-party, yet can still be verified remotely by a light client with limited resources. It works by requiring third-parties to produce succinct proofs of their computations: "succinct" because they can be verified using only a fraction of the proving time. We will explore two constructions, "Rollup" and "Rollup Non-Custodial", which use SNARKs (succinct non-interactive arguments of knowledge) to verifiably outsource computation on the blockchain.\n\nSpeaker Profile\n\nYing Tong is a Physics graduate student at NUS. She also works as a researcher at the Centre for Quantum Technologies and the Ethereum Foundation. She's interested in cryptography, p2p and privacy.\n\nEvent Page: https://www.meetup.com/NUSHackers/events/266209949/\n\nRecorded on: 8 November 2019\nProduced by Engineers.SG\nRecorded by: NUS Hackers\n\nHelp us caption & translate this video!\n\nhttps://amara.org/v/CRbDq/	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/wdFUqopfPEY/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/wdFUqopfPEY/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/wdFUqopfPEY/hqdefault.jpg	2019-11-15 11:32:12.780411	2025-02-25 04:01:32.164251	\N	t	1	108
