3950	lQ__hkz76ds	PHP Singapore Podcast (Episode 1)	2020-02-03 15:38:40	Presenters:\n- Zion Ng (https://twitter.com/zionsg2015)\n- Woo Huiren (https://twitter.com/woohuiren)\n- Ryuta Hamasaki (https://twitter.com/avosalmon)\n- Michael Cheng (https://twitter.com/coderkungfu)\n- Jun Hao\n\nShow Notes:\n==========\n\n## 1. From Zend to Laminas - the future of Zend\n\nQuote from a blog article by Matthew Wei'er O'Phinney: "However, Rogue Wave has recently made a strategic decision to focus its efforts on the Zend Server product of the Zend portfolio."\n\nZend Framework has been moved out of Zend to become the Laminas Project.\n\nWill Zend continue its efforts on the Zend Engine after 2 acquisitions, seeing that it has let go of its community framework\n\nBlog articles:\n\n- From Zend to Laminas: https://framework.zend.com/blog/2019-04-17-announcing-laminas.html\n- From Zend Framework To The Laminas Project: https://mwop.net/blog/2019-04-17-from-zend-to-laminas.html\n- The Future of Zend Framework: https://mwop.net/blog/2018-10-17-long-live-zf.html\n\nFramework urls:\n\n- https://framework.zend.com/\n- https://getlaminas.org/\n\nTimeline (https://www.zend.com/about):\n\n- 2019: Perforce acquires Rogue Wave and the company becomes ""Zend by Perforce""\n- 2015: Rogue Wave acquires Zend\n\n## 2. PHP in 2020\n\nWe discussed about the blog article "PHP in 2020" at https://stitcher.io/blog/php-in-2020\n\nReminds us of "PHP: The Right Way" (https://phptherightway.com/)\n\n## 3. PHP RFC Highlights\n\n- https://wiki.php.net/rfc/negative_array_index\n- https://wiki.php.net/rfc/jit\n- https://wiki.php.net/rfc/weak_maps\n- https://wiki.php.net/rfc/class_name_literal_on_object (voted)\n\r\nProduced by Engineers.SG	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lQ__hkz76ds/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lQ__hkz76ds/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lQ__hkz76ds/hqdefault.jpg	2020-02-03 16:31:31.841213	2025-02-22 08:01:36.356734	\N	t	1	168
