803	WAznFdX1O4g	Secrets of Testing Rails 5 Apps - RedDotRubyConf 2016	2016-06-26 04:55:00	Speaker: Prathamesh Sonpatki, Director, BigBinary LLC\n\nTesting Rails 5 apps has become better experience out of the box. Rails has also become smarter by introducing the test runner. Now we can't complain that about not able to run a single test or not getting coloured output. A lot of effort gone into making tests especially integration tests run faster. Come and join me as we will commence the journey to uncover the secrets of testing Rails 5 apps.\n\nSpeaker's Bio\nPrathamesh is Director at BigBinary. He builds web apps using Rails and React.js!. He is interested in open source and contribute to many Ruby and Rails related projects. He likes Emacs operating system a lot and can be found constantly tweaking his .emacs.d\n\nEvent Page: http://www.reddotrubyconf.com/\n\nProduced by Engineers.SG\n\nHelp us caption & translate this video!\n\nhttp://amara.org/v/ONq1/	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/WAznFdX1O4g/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/WAznFdX1O4g/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/WAznFdX1O4g/hqdefault.jpg	2016-06-26 04:59:38.707646	2024-12-20 04:01:01.90502	\N	t	1	2207
1189	CZF7VNvV6CI	Test Driving a React.js UI Component with Jasmine - Agile Singapore Conference 2016	2016-10-17 18:13:51	Speaker: Naresh Jain (@nashjain), Founder @ ConfEngine.com\n\nOver the past decade, eXtreme Programming practices like Test-Driven Development (TDD) & Behaviour Driven Developer (BDD), Refactoring, Continuous Integration and Automation have fundamentally changed software development processes and inherently how engineers work. While TDD has seen a great adoption on server side, developers still find it hard to apply TDD for developing UI components.\n\nIn code walk-thru where Naresh will build a web commenting and discussion feature (like Disqus) in React.js, 100% test driven. He will also demonstrate how TDD will help us drive an object-functional design to strike a pragmatic balance between the Object-Oriented and Functional Programming paradigms.\n\nSlides: https://www.slideshare.net/slideshow/embed_code/key/bbViCfdyQE0wlP?feature=oembed\n\nEvent Page: http://2016.agilesingapore.org\n\nProduced by Engineers.SG\n\nHelp us caption & translate this video!\n\nhttp://amara.org/v/XvTE/	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/CZF7VNvV6CI/default.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/CZF7VNvV6CI/mqdefault.jpg	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/CZF7VNvV6CI/hqdefault.jpg	2016-10-17 18:15:50.086392	2025-01-26 15:00:56.115406	\N	t	1	284
